2026-10-12 13:30:20 UTC — Primary-calendar date utility and event-label color handling

Actions:
- Corrected the previous color interpretation: Google Calendar events expose modern `eventLabelId` values separately from legacy `colorId`. The earlier answer looked only at legacy IDs and calendar palette, which was not the event's visible label color.
- Verified today's primary-calendar events through `eventLabelId` plus `Calendar.labelProperties.eventLabels`; their order is Cobalt, Pistachio, Birch, Cobalt, Grape. Known label colors map to `#4285f4`, `#7cb342`, `#a79b8e`, and `#8e24aa` respectively.
- Added `skills/productivity/google-workspace/scripts/calendar_day.py`: fetches one ISO date from primary calendar `primary` (Theodore), defaults to Asia/Singapore, supports an explicit IANA timezone, uses a half-open local-day interval, follows all event pages, excludes cancelled/declined entries, and returns event-label/legacy/calendar-default color data.
- Updated the Google Workspace skill with usage examples and synchronized the new script and instructions into the active installed skill; verified the copies match.
- Added unit tests for timezone windows, label and legacy color resolution, primary-only querying, pagination, and calendar-default color fallback.

Verification:
- `scripts/run_tests.sh tests/skills/test_google_calendar_day.py tests/skills/test_google_workspace_api.py tests/skills/test_google_workspace_setup.py -q` — 26 passed, 0 failed.
